Source: sgi-l1-usb-control
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Stuart Shelton <stuart@shelton.me>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libncurses-dev, pkgconf
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: sgi-l1-usb-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: adduser, dkms, udev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: DKMS driver for SGI L1 USB system controllers
 This package installs the sgi_l1_usb out-of-tree kernel module source for
 DKMS.  The module exposes the legacy SGI sgil1 raw USB transport devices for
 L1/L3 system controller communication.

Package: sgil1ctl
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: utility for SGI L1 USB transport diagnostics
 sgil1ctl reads status/configuration from the sgi_l1_usb driver and provides
 L1 status, power, log, LED, and raw protocol diagnostic commands without a
 terminal-library dependency.

Package: sgil1ctl-tui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: sgil1ctl (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: sgil1ctl
Replaces: sgil1ctl
Description: utility for SGI L1 USB transport diagnostics with TUI
 This edition of sgil1ctl includes the optional ncurses split-pane interface
 for combined L1 log and diagnostic LED monitoring. It otherwise provides the
 same command-line interface as the minimal sgil1ctl package.
